# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Maximum Independent Set problem {#the-maximum-independent-set-problem}"
msgstr "Ang Maximum Independent Set problem {#the-maximum-independent-set-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Maximum Independent Set (MIS) problem is a fundamental challenge in combinatorial optimization.\n"
"Formally, given a graph $G(V, E)$, the goal is to find the largest subset of vertices $V_I \\subset V$ such that no two vertices in $V_I$ are connected by an edge, as in $\\nexists (u, v) \\in E : v \\in V_I \\wedge u \\in V_I$.\n"
"Each vertex is assigned a binary decision variable $x_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}$, and a constraint $x_u + x_v \\leq 1$ is introduced for every edge, ensuring that at most one endpoint of each edge is selected.\n"
"The problem can thus be stated as the following maximization problem:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\max_{x_i} \\sum_{i \\in V} x_i \\qquad\\text{(find the largest set)}\\\\\n"
"\\text{s.t.} \\quad x_u + x_v \\leq 1 \\quad \\forall (u, v) \\in E.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Maximum Independent Set (MIS) problem ay isang pangunahing hamon sa combinatorial optimization.\n"
"Formally, sa ibinigay na graph $G(V, E)$, ang layunin ay hanapin ang pinakamalaking subset ng vertices $V_I \\subset V$ kung saan walang dalawang vertex sa $V_I$ na konektado ng isang edge, tulad ng $\\nexists (u, v) \\in E : v \\in V_I \\wedge u \\in V_I$.\n"
"Bawat vertex ay binibigyan ng binary decision variable $x_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}$, at isang constraint $x_u + x_v \\leq 1$ ay ipinapasok para sa bawat edge, para matiyak na hindi hihigit sa isang endpoint ng bawat edge ang mapipili.\n"
"Sa gayon, maaaring sabihin ang problema bilang sumusunod na maximization problem:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\max_{x_i} \\sum_{i \\in V} x_i \\qquad\\text{(hanapin ang pinakamalaking set)}\\\\\n"
"\\text{s.t.} \\quad x_u + x_v \\leq 1 \\quad \\forall (u, v) \\in E.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "MIS has a wide range of practical applications. In wireless network planning, an independent set corresponds to a group of transmitters that can all broadcast simultaneously without mutual interference. In scheduling, it models the largest collection of tasks that can execute concurrently given pairwise resource conflicts. In computational biology, it captures sets of mutually non-interacting proteins in a network.\n"
msgstr "Malawak ang praktikal na aplikasyon ng MIS. Sa wireless network planning, ang independent set ay tumutugma sa isang grupo ng mga transmitter na maaaring lahat mag-broadcast nang sabay-sabay nang walang mutual interference. Sa scheduling, minomodelo nito ang pinakamalaking koleksyon ng mga task na maaaring maisagawa nang sabay-sabay kahit may pairwise resource conflicts. Sa computational biology, hinuhuli nito ang mga set ng mutually non-interacting proteins sa isang network.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Despite its intuitive formulation, MIS is NP-hard, and even for graphs with a few hundred nodes specific instances become difficult to solve exactly or heuristically [\\[2\\]](#references).\n"
"The problem also gives rise to sparse constraint structures that are well suited for hardware implementations of quantum optimization, making it an attractive benchmark for near-term quantum devices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa kabila ng intuitive na formulation nito, ang MIS ay NP-hard, at kahit para sa mga graph na may ilang daang nodes, nagiging mahirap lutasin nang eksakto o heuristically ang ilang partikular na instance [\\[2\\]](#references).\n"
"Ang problema ay nagbibigay din ng sparse constraint structures na angkop para sa hardware implementations ng quantum optimization, kaya't ito ay naging kaakit-akit na benchmark para sa near-term quantum devices.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Aqarios Constrained Quantum Optimizer {#aqarios-constrained-quantum-optimizer}"
msgstr "Aqarios Constrained Quantum Optimizer {#aqarios-constrained-quantum-optimizer}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The standard approach to embedding a constrained binary problem into quantum optimization transforms the model into an unconstrained format by adding penalty terms: each violated constraint $x_u + x_v \\leq 1$ contributes $2 x_u x_v$ to the minimization objective $-\\sum_i x_i$. This is handled automatically by the Constrained Quantum Optimizer Qiskit Function.\n"
msgstr "Ang standard approach para i-embed ang isang constrained binary problem sa quantum optimization ay nagbabago sa model tungo sa unconstrained format sa pamamagitan ng pagdagdag ng penalty terms: ang bawat nilabag na constraint $x_u + x_v \\leq 1$ ay nag-aambag ng $2 x_u x_v$ sa minimization objective $-\\sum_i x_i$. Ito ay awtomatikong hinahawakan ng Constrained Quantum Optimizer Qiskit Function.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Beyond this standard transformation, the optimizer identifies **cliques** in the constraint graph. A clique is a set of nodes $V_C$ where every pair of nodes shares an edge. As a consequence, the $\\binom{|V_C|}{2}$ pairwise constraints $x_u + x_v \\leq 1 \\;\\forall (u,v) \\in E_C$ can be replaced by a single, tighter constraint $\\sum_{i \\in V_C} x_i \\leq 1$. Introducing a slack variable $y$ turns this into an equality $\\sum_i x_i + y = 1$, which takes the form of a one-hot constraint that can be enforced directly in QAOA using **XY-mixers** [\\[3\\]](#references). This reduces the search space and avoids the need for penalty terms for those constraints, improving solution quality.\n"
msgstr "Higit pa sa standard transformation na ito, tinutukoy ng optimizer ang mga **cliques** sa constraint graph. Ang clique ay isang set ng mga node $V_C$ kung saan ang bawat pares ng node ay may shared na edge. Bunga nito, ang $\\binom{|V_C|}{2}$ pairwise constraints $x_u + x_v \\leq 1 \\;\\forall (u,v) \\in E_C$ ay maaaring palitan ng iisang, mas mahigpit na constraint $\\sum_{i \\in V_C} x_i \\leq 1$. Ang pagpapakilala ng slack variable $y$ ay nagpapalit nito sa equality $\\sum_i x_i + y = 1$, na kumukuha ng anyo ng one-hot constraint na maaaring direktang i-enforce sa QAOA gamit ang **XY-mixers** [\\[3\\]](#references). Binabawasan nito ang search space at iniiwasan ang pangangailangan ng penalty terms para sa mga constraint na iyon, na nagpapabuti sa kalidad ng solusyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additionally, variables connected to only a single neighbor are called **pendant** nodes and are fixed deterministically by the algorithm before quantum execution, further reducing the effective problem size.\n"
msgstr "Bukod dito, ang mga variable na konektado lamang sa iisang neighbor ay tinatawag na **pendant** nodes at ito ay deterministikong ini-fix ng algorithm bago ang quantum execution, na lalong nagpapababa sa effective problem size.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Constrained Quantum Optimizer employs an **iterative warm-starting** approach compatible with XY-mixers [\\[1\\]](#references), which progressively narrows the search space by biasing the quantum state distribution towards promising solution regions across iterations. This enables the use of **fixed-angle QAOA parameters**, eliminating the need for variational parameter training. The total quantum resource requirements are governed solely by the number of warm-start iterations, which means the quantum cost straightforward to control.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang Constrained Quantum Optimizer ng **iterative warm-starting** approach na compatible sa XY-mixers [\\[1\\]](#references), na paunti-unting nagpapaliit sa search space sa pamamagitan ng pag-bias sa quantum state distribution patungo sa mga promising na solution regions sa bawat iteration. Ito ay nagbibigay-daan sa paggamit ng **fixed-angle QAOA parameters**, na inaalis ang pangangailangan para sa variational parameter training. Ang kabuuang quantum resource requirements ay dikta lamang ng bilang ng warm-start iterations, na nangangahulugang diretso lang i-control ang quantum cost.\n"

